    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive configuration for today is headlined by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, whose 73.66 rating marks the highest efficiency projection on the slate. His outlook is bolstered by a massive 14% park factor boost and a favorable platoon matchup against Hughes, making him our primary offensive anchor. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** (68.63) and **Drake Baldwin** (66.52) provide elite upside from the top of their respective lineups, taking full advantage of soft matchups against Kelly and King. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** (66.18) remains a high-floor start despite a more challenging encounter with Nola, as his base projection provides the stability we need in the outfield.\n\nPlatoon advantages and environmental variables have shifted several of our middle-tier decisions. **Coby Mayo** (59.20) benefits from a rare favorable split against a left-handed pitcher and a \"Slow SP Delivery\" tag, which significantly enhances his stolen base probability\u2014a critical factor given the extreme scarcity of that category in our league. Conversely, **Gunnar Henderson** (57.50) faces a slight regression due to the negative platoon impact against Rivera, but he remains locked in for his potential to contribute across all categories. In the outfield, **Wade Meckler** (46.46) earns his spot largely due to wind conditions blowing out, providing enough efficiency to edge out our bench options.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Nasim Nunez**, who fell just short of the cut with a score of 53.27. While **Nasim Nunez** benefits from the same favorable park factors as **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, his projection was suppressed by a lower batting order position, which ultimately tipped the scales in favor of our active starters. Looking ahead, managers should monitor the winds at **Heliot Ramos**\u2019s venue; while he is currently projected for a solid 56.89, the \"Wind In\" warning has already resulted in a 5% downward adjustment to his efficiency. We are navigating a slate where we must prioritize high-OBP and sprint-speed profiles like those of **Jacob Wilson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 standings.",
